G3824.b:
*† ⟪παλινγενεσία⟫ (Rec. παλιγγ-), -ας, ἡ
(< πάλιν, γένεσις), ⟪new birth⟫, ⟪renewal⟫, ⟪restoration⟫, ⟪regeneration⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of persons (Plut., Phil., al.), of spiritual regeneration, διὰ λουτροῦ παλινγενεστίας (gen. attr., v. Ellic., in l.), ⟦Titus 3:5|Tit 3:5⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of the world, as in Stoics, Jewish Apocal., al. (v. Dalman, Words, 177 ff.), ⟦Matthew 19:28|Mt 19:28⟧.†

G3835.b:
⟪πανοῦργος⟫, -ον,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨עָרוּם⁩;] ⟪ready to do anything⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ in cl., chiefly in bad sense, ⟪knavish⟫, ⟪crafty⟫: ⟦2 Corinthians 12:16|II Co 12:16⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ in good sense, ⟪skilful⟫, ⟪clever⟫ (⟦Proverbs 13:1|Pr 13:1⟧ ⟦Proverbs 28:2|28:2⟧).†

G3843.b:
⟪πάντως⟫, adv.
(< πάς), [in LXX: ⟦2 Kings 5:11|IV Ki 5:11⟧ (v. Thackeray, Gr., 47), To 14:8, al.;] ⟪altogether⟫, ⟪by all means⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ without neg. (from Hdt. on): ⟦1 Corinthians 16:12|I Co 16:12⟧; esp. in strong affirmations, ⟪surely⟫, ⟪at all events⟫: ⟦Luke 4:23|Lk 4:23⟧, ⟦Acts 21:22|Ac 21:22⟧ ⟦Acts 28:4|28:4⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 9:10|I Co 9:10⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ c. neg. (so always in Hom.), in a complete negation: ⟦Romans 3:9|Ro 3:9⟧; in a partial negation (Bl., § 75, 7), ⟦1 Corinthians 5:10|I Co 5:10⟧.†

G3844.b:
⟪παρά⟫, prep. c. gen., dat., acc., with radical sense, ⟪beside⟫.
⟪I.⟫ C. gen. pers., ⟪from the side of⟫, ⟪from beside⟫, ⟪from⟫, indicating source or origin, [in LXX for ⁨מֵאֵצֶל⁩, ⁨מִיַד⁩, ⁨מִלִּפְנֵי⁩;] after verbs of motion, ⟦Mark 14:43|Mk 14:43⟧, ⟦Luke 8:49|Lk 8:49⟧, ⟦John 15:26|Jo 15:26⟧, al.; after verbs of seeking, receiving, hearing, etc., ⟦Mark 8:11|Mk 8:11⟧ ⟦Mark 12:2|12:2⟧, ⟦John 4:9|Jo 4:9⟧, ⟦John 4:52|52⟧ ⟦John 10:18|10:18⟧, ⟦Philippians 4:18|Phl 4:18⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 1:18|II Ti 1:18⟧, ⟦James 1:7|Ja 1:7⟧, al.; after passive verbs, of the agent (like ὑπό), ⟦Matthew 21:42|Mt 21:42⟧, ⟦Mark 12:11|Mk 12:11⟧, ⟦Luke 1:37|Lk 1:37⟧; absol., οἱ παρ’ αὐτοῦ, ⟪his family⟫, ⟪his kinsfolk⟫, ⟦Mark 3:21|Mk 3:21⟧ (cf. M, Pr., 106 f.; Field, Notes, 25 f.; Swete, in l.); τὰ παρ’ αὐτῆς (αὐτῶν, ὑμῶν), ⟪one's means⟫, ⟪wealth⟫, ⟦Mark 5:26|Mk 5:26⟧, ⟦Luke 10:7|Lk 10:7⟧, ⟦Philippians 4:18|Phl 4:18⟧.
⟪II.⟫ C. dat. pers. (exc. ⟦John 19:25|Jo 19:25⟧, π. τ. σταυρῷ), ⟪by the side of⟫, ⟪beside⟫, ⟪by⟫, ⟪with⟫, [in LXX for ⁨בְּעֵינֵי⁩, ⁨בְּיַד⁩, ⁨אֵצֶל⁩;] ⟦Luke 11:37|Lk 11:37⟧ ⟦Luke 19:7|19:7⟧, ⟦John 1:40|Jo 1:40⟧ ⟦John 4:40|4:40⟧, ⟦Acts 28:14|Ac 28:14⟧, al.; παρ’ ἑαυτῷ, ⟪at home⟫, ⟦1 Corinthians 16:2|I Co 16:2⟧; c. dat. pl., ⟪among⟫, ⟦Matthew 22:25|Mt 22:25⟧, ⟦Colossians 4:16|Col 4:16⟧, al.; metaph., ⟦Matthew 19:26|Mt 19:26⟧, ⟦Mark 10:27|Mk 10:27⟧, ⟦Luke 1:30|Lk 1:30⟧, ⟦Romans 2:13|Ro 2:13⟧, ⟦James 1:27|Ja 1:27⟧, al.
⟪III.⟫ C. acc., of motion by or towards, [in LXX for ⁨בְּעֵבֶר ,עַל יַד ,אֵצֶל⁩;]
	⟪1.⟫ of place, ⟪by the side of⟫, ⟪beside⟫, ⟪by⟫, ⟪along⟫: ⟦Acts 10:32|Ac 10:32⟧, ⟦Hebrews 11:12|He 11:12⟧; after verbs of motion, ⟦Matthew 4:18|Mt 4:18⟧, ⟦Mark 4:4|Mk 4:4⟧, ⟦Luke 8:5|Lk 8:5⟧, ⟦Acts 4:35|Ac 4:35⟧, al.; after verbs of rest, ⟦Matthew 13:1|Mt 13:1⟧, ⟦Mark 5:21|Mk 5:21⟧, ⟦Luke 8:35|Lk 8:35⟧, al.
	⟪2.⟫ ⟪beside⟫, ⟪beyond⟫, metaph.;
		⟪(a)⟫ ⟪beyond⟫, ⟪against⟫, ⟪contrary to⟫: ⟦Acts 18:13|Ac 18:13⟧, ⟦Romans 1:26|Ro 1:26⟧ ⟦Romans 4:18|4:18⟧ ⟦Romans 11:24|11:24⟧, al.; ⟪except⟫, ⟦2 Corinthians 11:24|II Co 11:24⟧;
		⟪(b)⟫ ⟪beyond⟫, ⟪above⟫, ⟪in comparison with⟫: ⟦Luke 3:13|Lk 3:13⟧, ⟦Romans 12:3|Ro 12:3⟧ ⟦Romans 14:5|14:5⟧, ⟦Hebrews 1:4|He 1:4⟧, ⟦Hebrews 1:9|9⟧ ⟦Hebrews 3:3|3:3⟧, al.;
		⟪(c)⟫ ⟪on account of⟫: ⟦1 Corinthians 12:15|I Co 12:15⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:16|16⟧.
⟪IV.⟫ In composition: ⟪beside⟫, ⟪to⟫ (παραλαμβάνω, παράγω), ⟪at hand⟫ (πάρειμι), ⟪from⟫ (παραρρέω), ⟪amiss⟫ (παρακούω), ⟪past⟫ (παρέρχομαι), ⟪compared with⟫ (παρομοιάζω), ⟪above measure⟫ (παροργίζω).

G3858.b:
⟪παρα-δέχομαι⟫,
[in LXX: ⟦Exodus 23:1|Ex 23:1⟧ (⁨נשׂא⁩), ⟦Proverbs 3:12|Pr 3:12⟧ (⁨רצה⁩), II Mac 4:22 R, III Mac 7:12*;] ⟪to receive⟫, ⟪admit⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ of things: ⟦Mark 4:20|Mk 4:20⟧, ⟦Acts 15:4|Ac 15:4⟧ ⟦Acts 16:21|16:21⟧ ⟦Acts 22:18|22:18⟧, ⟦1 Timothy 5:19|I Ti 5:19⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ of persons: ⟦Hebrews 12:6|He 12:6⟧(LXX).†

G3877.b:
** ⟪παρ-ακολουθέω⟫, -ῶ,
[in LXX: II Mac 8:11 9:27 R*;] c. dat., ⟪to follow closely⟫, ⟪accompany⟫. Metaph., in various senses,
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to result⟫: ⟦Mark 16:17|Mk 16:[17]⟧;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to follow up⟫, ⟪trace⟫, ⟪investigate⟫: ⟦Luke 1:3|Lk 1:3⟧ (so freq. in cl.);
⟪(c)⟫ ⟪to follow⟫ as a standard of conduct: ⟦1 Timothy 4:6|I Ti 4:6⟧, ⟦2 Timothy 3:10|II Ti 3:10⟧. (For exx. from π., v. MM, xviii.)†

G3881.b:
* ⟪παρα-λέγω⟫, ⟪to lay beside⟫; mid.,
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to lie beside⟫ (Hom.);
⟪(b)⟫ later, of sailors, ⟪to sail past⟫: c. acc., ⟦Acts 27:8|Ac 27:8⟧, ⟦Acts 27:13|13⟧.†
